    A reference act carries — implicitly or explicitly — an expected cardinality: how many referents the actor means to pick out. Part of the act's type, knowable before any resolution, and what gives a miss its meaning.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:\{n,m\} \in \{\{1,1\},\{0,1\},\{0,N\},\{1,N\}\}>
    :reading The four bounds; same descriptors + same world + different bound = different meaning of the same result. One axis, four sites (suffix sugar, paths, schema, the type algebra's exponents).
